Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Standard::AllocateOptimal: an allocation that fails throws
Standard_OutOfMemory, as Standard::Allocate, Standard::Reallocate and the
flexible memory manager do. With the native (default), TBB and jemalloc
memory managers it returned null, and its callers (NCollection_Allocator,
so NCollection_Array1 and every collection on it, NCollection_IncAllocator,
the packed and sparse maps, the strings) wrote to the block at once: under
a memory limit the shape checker crashed in CSLib_Class2d (the polygon of a
face's wire, BRepTopAdaptor_FClass2d) writing to an array whose allocation
had failed. Standard_Failure's message, the one caller that checked for
null, catches the exception and goes without the message as before.

Standard_OutOfMemory::NbRaised: how many of these exceptions the process
has constructed. The checker and the shape healing catch Standard_Failure
inside (a sub-shape whose check failed is invalid), so an allocation that
failed under them may not reach their caller; it compares the count before
and after the call.
diff --git a/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Standard/Standard.cxx b/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Standard/Standard.cxx
index bddca3e..d898d78 100644
--- a/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Standard/Standard.cxx
+++ b/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Standard/Standard.cxx
@@ -398,12 +398,22 @@ void* Standard::AllocateOptimal(const size_t theSize)
 {
 #ifdef OCCT_MMGT_OPT_FLEXIBLE
   return Standard_MMgrFactory::GetMMgr()->Allocate(theSize);
-#elif defined OCCT_MMGT_OPT_JEMALLOC
-  return je_malloc(theSize);
-#elif defined OCCT_MMGT_OPT_TBB
-  return scalable_malloc(theSize);
 #else
-  return malloc(theSize);
+  // As Allocate() and the flexible memory manager: callers (the collections'
+  // allocators, strings) write to the block at once, so a failed allocation
+  // must not return null.
+  #if defined OCCT_MMGT_OPT_JEMALLOC
+  void* aPtr = je_malloc(theSize);
+  #elif defined OCCT_MMGT_OPT_TBB
+  void* aPtr = scalable_malloc(theSize);
+  #else
+  void* aPtr = malloc(theSize);
+  #endif
+  if (aPtr == nullptr && theSize != 0)
+  {
+    throw Standard_OutOfMemory("Standard::AllocateOptimal(): malloc failed");
+  }
+  return aPtr;
 #endif
 }
 
